:: StoryTitle
Cellar Door


:: StoryData
{
  "ifid": "7C1B2D34-5E6F-4A70-8B91-A2B3C4D5E6F7",
  "format": "SugarCube",
  "format-version": "2.37.3",
  "start": "Stairs"
}


:: StoryInit
<<set $lantern to false>>
<<set $matches to 3>>
<<set $name to "stranger">>


:: StoryCaption
Matches left: $matches


:: Widgets [widget]
<<widget "creak">>The boards creak underfoot.<</widget>>


:: Stairs
/* The opening passage. */
<<playSound "wind" 0.4>>
The cellar stairs go down further than the house is tall.
Someone has chalked a word on the wall, //twice//: $name.
<<if $lantern>>
The lantern throws your shadow ahead of you.
<<elseif $matches gte 2>>
You still have matches enough for the way back.
<<else>>
It is very dark.
<</if>>
[[Go down|Landing][$matches -= 1]]
<<link "Light the lantern" "Stairs">><<set $lantern to true>>The match flares.<</link>>
<<if $matches is 0>>[[Give up|Outside]]<</if>>


:: Landing
<<set $knocked to true>>
<<creak>>
A door waits at the bottom, painted the colour of old tea.
You have <<print $matches>> matches left.
<<textbox "$name" "stranger">>
<<switch $matches>>
<<case 0>>
You will have to find the handle by touch.
<<case 1 2>>
One more match, maybe two.
<<default>>
Plenty of light, for now.
<</switch>>
<<notify>>The door is not locked.<</notify>>
<<set $matches to 5>>
<<if $lantern>><<goto "Cellar">><</if>>
[[Open the door|Cellar]]
[[Go back up|Stairs]]


:: Cellar
<<set _count to 2>>
<<set $name to "the one who opened the door">>
Shelves, jars, and a smell of apples.
<<if $knocked>>Nobody answered your knock, and nobody is here.<</if>>
<<back>>


:: Outside
The night air is cold and the house is quiet behind you.
[[Try again|Crossroads]]


:: Crossroads
<<set $lantern to false>>
[[Stairs]]
[[Take the short way|Shortcut]]


:: Shortcut
<<goto "Outside">>
